                <pb facs="0293" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg181"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 T 71/152: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >White</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-10T09:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1919,
                                9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 13, 10
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>125. Russian diplomatic officer Askhabad telegraphs that the Bolsheviks state
                    that Consul Tredwell desires following message dated Tashkent March 27th be
                    transmitted to you: <pb facs="0294" n="182" xml:id="pg182"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I am leaving today for Moscow with the Danish and Swedish Missions,
                            having been released by the local authorities. Health good. Hope to see
                            my family soon again, please greet them for me.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
